course: dictionary
lesson: 4797
title: The humerus
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The humerus is a bone. It is the long bone in the top part of your arm, between your shoulder and your elbow.
explain: Your forearm has two more bones, the radius and the ulna, which run from your elbow down to your wrist. In a skeleton diagram, the humerus is the single long bone above the elbow.
explain: Humerus is a noun, and it can change to show more than one: one humerus, two humeri. When you read «The upper arm bone is the humerus», the word is simply the name of that bone.
fact: The humerus is the long bone in the upper arm.
fact: It runs from the shoulder to the elbow.
fact: The plural of humerus is humeri.
fact: The funny bone is not a bone at all: it is a nerve near the elbow end of the humerus.
fact: «Funny bone» is a joke on humerus and humorous, because bumping that nerve sends a zinging feeling down the arm.
exercise: Where is the humerus? | *In the upper arm, between the shoulder and the elbow | In the neck, between the head and the shoulders | In the hand, between the fingers | In the leg, between the knee and the hip
exercise: «The upper arm bone is the humerus.» What is the plural of humerus? | humeruses | humerii | *humeri | humerae
exercise: The funny bone is really what? | A muscle in the back | A tiny bone in the little finger | *A nerve near the elbow end of the humerus | A joke book from the library
test: Which two bones make up the forearm, from the elbow to the wrist? | *radius and ulna | humerus and femur | skull and spine | ribs and collarbone
test: Why is it called the funny bone? | It is shaped like a smile | *It is a pun on humerus and humorous | It was named by a comedian | It is the smallest bone in the arm
exam: Which word is the name of the long bone between the shoulder and the elbow? | radius | femur | ulna | *humerus
